WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.425
In some ways life at Birtwick Park was a lot like life at Farmer Grey's.

2
00:00:08.426 --> 00:00:12.544
The people were kind, and I had plenty to eat and drink.

3
00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:16.786
I was frequently ridden and hitched to the carriage.

4
00:00:16.787 --> 00:00:19.270
But in other ways, things were different.

5
00:00:19.271 --> 00:00:23.433
For one thing, I wasn't hitched beside my mother anymore.

6
00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:27.547
My new partner was Ginger, the tall chestnut mare.

7
00:00:27.548 --> 00:00:32.064
The first time we were hitched together, I couldn't help being worried.

8
00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:34.594
What if we didn't get along?

9
00:00:34.595 --> 00:00:39.201
What if she wouldn't pull her share of the weight?

10
00:00:39.202 --> 00:00:43.988
As soon as we got started, I felt much better.

11
00:00:43.989 --> 00:00:46.264
Ginger was an honest worker.

12
00:00:46.265 --> 00:00:51.119
She did her full share of the work, even while going uphill.

13
00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.077
In fact, we made a good team!

14
00:00:54.078 --> 00:00:58.347
At first she didn't have much to say to me.

15
00:00:58.348 --> 00:01:03.833
But after we'd been out together a few times, we started to become friends.

16
00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:07.763
Merrylegs and I were friends from the first day I arrived.

17
00:01:07.764 --> 00:01:13.133
He was so cheerful, friendly, and sociable that he made me feel right at home.

18
00:01:13.134 --> 00:01:20.489
The squire's daughters, Jessie and Flora, came to visit him almost every day.

19
00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:26.917
They loved to ride him around the orchard or take him driving.

20
00:01:26.918 --> 00:01:29.947
There were also two other horses on the estate.

21
00:01:29.948 --> 00:01:36.350
They lived in a different part of the stable, but sometimes we all grazed together in the orchard.

22
00:01:36.351 --> 00:01:39.264
The first horse was called Justice.

23
00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:44.442
He was a sturdy horse who was used for riding and driving.

24
00:01:44.443 --> 00:01:48.213
The second was Sir Oliver, an elderly brown horse.

25
00:01:48.214 --> 00:01:51.622
He was too old to work much anymore.

26
00:01:51.623 --> 00:01:58.956
But he was so gentle and reliable that the squire sometimes used him to carry one of his daughters when the whole family rode together.

27
00:01:58.957 --> 00:02:03.619
Sir Oliver was just as careful with the little girls as Merrylegs himself.

28
00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:09.890
As I said, I got to know these two when all the horses were put out together in the old orchard.

29
00:02:09.891 --> 00:02:14.010
Sadly, though, this didn't happen nearly often enough for me.

30
00:02:14.011 --> 00:02:18.384
That was the biggest change of all in my life at Birtwick Park.

31
00:02:18.385 --> 00:02:25.319
For my first four years, I got to run and play as much as I liked in my pleasant field.

32
00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:29.147
But now I spent most of my time standing in my stall.

33
00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:34.957
It was large and airy, but it was still boring compared to that big, grassy field.

34
00:02:34.958 --> 00:02:39.921
I only got to go out in the orchard once a week or so.

35
00:02:39.922 --> 00:02:45.342
I don't mean to complain. James, John, and the squire treated me very well.

36
00:02:45.343 --> 00:02:50.221
But I was a young horse with a lot of energy and spirit.

37
00:02:50.222 --> 00:02:54.753
I was used to being able to gallop around whenever I felt the urge.

38
00:02:54.754 --> 00:02:59.847
Now I had to stay still and behave myself no matter how much energy I had.

39
00:02:59.848 --> 00:03:02.611
It was very difficult sometimes!

40
00:03:02.612 --> 00:03:07.977
John was usually the one to exercise me when the squire didn't need me himself.

41
00:03:07.978 --> 00:03:13.209
One day when he saddled me up, I was feeling extra lively.

42
00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:18.160
I hadn't had much exercise that week, and it was almost impossible to stay quiet.

43
00:03:18.161 --> 00:03:21.868
I couldn't help prancing as soon as John mounted.

44
00:03:21.869 --> 00:03:25.330
"Steady, my boy," he said with a laugh.

45
00:03:25.331 --> 00:03:31.487
"Let's just get out of the stable yard, and then I'll let you trot, all right?"

46
00:03:31.488 --> 00:03:34.276
I was almost bursting out of my skin.

47
00:03:34.277 --> 00:03:38.000
But I stayed at a prancing walk as he rode me out of the yard.

48
00:03:38.001 --> 00:03:42.674
Once we reached a quiet lane, he let me move into a brisk trot.

49
00:03:42.675 --> 00:03:44.497
That was better!

50
00:03:44.498 --> 00:03:50.698
I surged forward eagerly, and after a few miles, I felt much calmer.

51
00:03:50.699 --> 00:03:56.029
"There you go, Black Beauty." John gave me a pat as he brought me back to a walk.

52
00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:58.423
"I think you needed that."

53
00:03:58.424 --> 00:04:03.733
He was right. I felt like a different horse, calm and content.

54
00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:09.381
I was happy to walk along quietly as he turned us back toward home.

55
00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:14.269
John kept talking to me as we rode. Or maybe he was talking to himself.

56
00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:17.247
It's sometimes hard to tell with people.

57
00:04:17.248 --> 00:04:21.295
Either way I pricked my ears to listen to his soothing voice.

58
00:04:21.296 --> 00:04:27.432
"A spirited horse like you isn't meant to stand around without enough exercise," John said.

59
00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:31.712
"Some people might see you prancing around and think you're a nervous horse.

60
00:04:31.713 --> 00:04:34.542
But I know that all you need is to move.

61
00:04:34.543 --> 00:04:39.697
After all that's what horses were made to do."

62
00:04:39.698 --> 00:04:45.923
Having to stand in my stall so much made me enjoy my time in the orchard even more.

63
00:04:45.924 --> 00:04:51.174
It was pleasant out there, with grass to nibble and shade from the old trees.

64
00:04:51.175 --> 00:04:54.413
Usually all the horses were turned out together.

65
00:04:54.414 --> 00:04:58.528
That gave me a chance to get to know the others better.

66
00:04:58.529 --> 00:05:09.484
And I soon discovered that they had some amazing, though sad, stories to tell— especially Ginger.

